# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[provide]] (a place) with a [[system]] of sewers.

===Etymology 2===
From {{inh|en|enm|seware}}, {{m|enm|seuere}}, from {{uder|en|xno|asseour}}, from {{uder|en|fro|asseoir||find a seat for}}, from {{uder|en|la|assidēre}}, present active infinitive of {{m|la|assideō||attend to}}, from {{m|la|ad||to, towards, at}} + {{m|la|sedeō||sit}}.

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|so͞o'ə|a=RP}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈs(j)uːə/}}
* {{enPR|so͞oər|a=GA}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈsuɚ/}}
** {{audio|en|LL-Q1860 (eng)-Vealhurl-sewer (j).wav|a=Southern England}}
* {{hyphenation|en|sew|er}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|historical}} An [[official]] in charge of a [[princely]] [[household]], also responsible for the [[ceremonial]] task of attending at dinners, seating the guests and serving dishes.
#* {{RQ:Scott Ivanhoe|volume=II|chapter=VII|pages=116–117|pageref=116|passage=While the Saxon was plunged in these painful reflections, the door of their prison opened, and gave entrance to a '''sewer''', holding his white rod of office.}}

===Etymology 3===
{{etymid|en|sews}} {{suffix|en|sew|er}}
[[File:Man sewing in Dhaka.jpg|A sewer (Etymology 3) in Dhaka|thumb|right]]

====Pronunciation====
* {{enPR|sō'ə|a=RP}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈsəʊə/}}
* {{enPR|sō'ər|a=US}}, {{IPA|en|/ˈsoʊɚ/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-sewer-2.ogg|a=US}}
* {{homophones|en|sower}}<!--one who sows-->
* {{rhymes|en|əʊə(ɹ)|s=2}}
* {{hyphenation|en|sew|er}}

====Noun====
{{en-noun}}

# One who [[sew]]s.
#* {{RQ:Riis Other Half|pages=131–132|pageref=131|passage=Up under the roof three men are making boys’ jackets at twenty cents a piece, of which the '''sewer''' takes eight, the ironer three, the finisher five cents, and the buttonhole-maker two and a quarter, leaving a cent and three-quarters to pay for the drumming up, the fetching and bringing back of the goods.}}
# A small [[tortricid]] [[moth]], the [[larva]] of which sews together the edges of a leaf using [[silk]].
#: {{ux|en|the apple-leaf '''sewer''', {{taxlink|Ancylis nubeculana|species}}}}

